*           per-account OS-access grants (ACC$SH, ACC$OS.EXEC) - the owner's
*           model: os.execute and shell off for anyone but administrators
*           unless given specifically. An administrator is refused (10039); the
*           grant takes effect at the account's next entry. See os.set.
* 09 Sep 26 PRE_RELEASE 18. The tier is settable - ADMINISTRATOR, PROGRAMMER,
*           STANDARD - which is the only way an EXISTING account can become an
*           administrator. CREATE.ACCOUNT refuses a name already in the
*           register (CREATEA:255, sysmsg 6002), so before this the advice
