* START-DESCRIPTION:
* MODIFY.ACCOUNT account <ADD/DELETE> user.name
* MODIFY.ACCOUNT account STANDARD | PROGRAMMER | ADMINISTRATOR
* MODIFY.ACCOUNT account SH-ON | SH-OFF | OS-ON | OS-OFF
*
* THE TIER FORM IS THE PORT'S GRAMMAR MINUS ONE VALUE.  SD Core for Windows has
* MODIFY.ACCOUNT account STANDARD | PROGRAMMER | ADMINISTRATOR | SUSPENDED
* (its gpl.bp/MODIFYA:121), and conformity with the port outranks conformity
* with upstream.  SUSPENDED IS LEFT OUT ON PURPOSE rather than forgotten: it is
* a denial of access, and the doors it has to close - LOGIN, CPROC's account
* entry, ssh - are PRE_RELEASE 13's work and are not built here.  A SUSPENDED
* that wrote a tier and shut no door would be a control that does not act.
*
* NO INTERMEDIATE STEP IS REQUIRED, matching the port: an account may go from
* any of the three to any other in one command.
*
* THE VOC FOLLOWS THE TIER AT ONCE (SL1, 10 Sep 26): STANDARD = NEWVOC less
* TIER.OMIT.STANDARD, PROGRAMMER = NEWVOC, ADMINISTRATOR = that plus
* TIER.ADD.ADMINISTRATOR from VOC_TEMPLATE - the sets CREATE.ACCOUNT builds.
* See voc.delta.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
